  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Brightness Temperature and Sea Ice Concentration from Nimbus-7",
  "description": "Sea ice concentration data set was derived from the dual-polarized 37-ghz channel radiances from the Nimbus-7 SMMR. Sea ice concentrations, i.e., fraction of ice cover in a 30 x 30 km field of view, are grouped in scenes, each covering an area of 780 x 780 km. This data set was derived from the cell-all tapes (NSSDC id 78-098a-08b), and there are six days of data per one or two tapes. These tapes are available from NSSDC A similar data set (map-30) containing six-day and monthly averages of 37-ghz horizontal polarization channel brightness temperatures projected on to 533 x 533 mercator map grids is also available from NSSDC. The map-30 data set was also generated from the cell-all tapes. No map-30 data were produced beyond year 5 (October 1983).\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: This data set was created for sea ice concentration, derived from the dual-polarized 37-ghz channel radiances from the Nimbus-7 SMMR. Sea ice concentrations, i.e., fraction of ice cover in a 30 x 30 km field of view, are grouped in scenes, each covering an area of 780 x 780 km.",
